          "case": "one",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "Statement of Local finiteness and Lorentz invariance of the scalar shell measure: Assume Countable Choice. For every $\\mu\\ge0$, the measure $d\\nu_\\mu$ of [[def-qft-scalar-mass-shell]] is locally finite and sigma-finite on $H_\\mu^+$. For every proper orthochronous Lorentz transformation $\\Lambda$ and every nonnegative Borel function $g$ on $H_\\mu^+$, $$\\int_{H_\\mu^+}g(\\Lambda^{-1}p)\\,d\\nu_\\mu(p) =\\int_{H_\\mu^+}g(p)\\,d\\nu_\\mu(p).$$ The claim applies off the omitted apex when $\\mu=0$. The objects have the fixed fiber, test domain, witness or shell specified there. This claim does not vary a finite set cardinality through a singleton boundary; any displayed unit scalar/vector is part of the stated data."
        },
