      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-38",
        "notes": "Checked all three steps and all seven direct suppliers. q_2 shell bound is integrable for every mu>=0: radial orders r, r^2 and r^-3 establish range membership. Rational-box supplier has real rational coefficients; local real/imaginary approximation and explicit Cantor pairing correctly establish complex L2 separability. Multiplication by sqrt(w_mu), with positive finite weight off the null apex, is a surjective isometry on equivalence classes. Annuli increase to full measure; subtracting monotone interior integrals from finite total gives tails tending to zero. Weight bounds on each annulus permit C_c^infinity approximation from the exact complex open-set density supplier. G=psi(q)rho(q0-omega(q)) extends smoothly by zero across the massless apex since psi vanishes near it, and has compact support; Fourier automorphism provides exact shell restriction. Melrose Theorem 9.1, printed p.58, checked. Reader additions explicitly close immediate integrability, complex typing and tail-limit details; no false current claim or substantial prerequisite gap found. Final scoped rendering found a multiline display in step 2.1; replaced the internal formula newline with a space without changing mathematics. Reflow reported unchanged thereafter. Final precheck and rendercheck passed, as did strict proof-contract checks after adding both F3 use mappings for step 1.1. This mechanical amendment adds no mathematical defect-ledger row."
