          "case": "empty",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "Statement of Continuity and Klein–Gordon annihilation of scalar shell restriction: Assume Countable Choice [[def-countable-choice]]. For every $\\mu\\ge0$, the pointwise restriction $$K_\\mu f(p)=\\int_{\\mathbb R^4}f(x)e^{ip\\circ x}\\,d^4x$$ of [[def-qft-scalar-mass-shell]] maps $\\mathscr S(\\mathbb R^4)$ continuously and linearly into $H_\\mu$. It also annihilates the Klein–Gordon test operator: $$K_\\mu\\bigl((\\partial_0^2-\\Delta+\\mu^2)f\\bigr)=0 \\qquad(f\\in\\mathscr S(\\mathbb R^4)).$$ The coordinates are the fixed length coordinates of that definition and $\\mu$ has inverse-length units. The specified witness, fixed coordinate space or supplied Hilbert/test objects are the inputs of this assertion; it does not assert a separate existence result after replacing them by an empty underlying set."
