      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-38",
        "notes": "Checked all three proof steps and four direct suppliers. Tensor product inner products give isometry on finite sums, inverse tensor powers give surjectivity, and permutation averaging preserves symmetric sectors. Zeroth sector is C and maps vacuum identically; H=0 and n=1 remain valid. Creation intertwining is symmetrized insertion, contraction intertwining follows from <Uh,Uv>_2=<h,v>_2 and bounded fixed-sector maps. Telescoping product estimate, density and the common unitary norm bound prove orbit continuity on each sector and then the direct sum for arbitrary topological parameter space G. AC_omega is explicit, with no stronger selection. Tong section 2.4 is only multiparticle context; general lift and continuity are locally proved. Accept reader topology/locator clarifications and layout; no mathematical defect confirmed."
      }
