      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-38",
        "notes": "Checked all four steps and eleven direct suppliers. The matrix subspace/product topology is metrizable and locally compact; proper future-preserving Lorentz inverse and determinant one meet all change-of-variables hypotheses. Repeated affine chain rule preserves each Schwartz seminorm. Invariant shell measure preserves null classes; inverse action gives surjectivity; Lorentz phase identity gives the semidirect group law. The complex Fourier change of variables follows from four nonnegative parts and absolute Schwartz integrability. For compactly supported chart h, images under a compact parameter neighborhood form a compact shell subset; for mu=0 it stays away from the apex since inverse Lorentz matrices are uniformly bounded. The finite-measure majorant therefore justifies dominated convergence along sequences, which suffices in this metrizable group; density and norm-one action extend continuity to all H_mu. No empirical premise; AC_omega retained. Tong/Srednicki support normalization only, and full Hilbert-space representation proof is local. Accept reader topology and complex-integral explanations and layout; no mathematical defect confirmed."
