      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-38",
        "notes": "Checked six complete proof paragraphs and all fifteen direct prerequisite statements; independently read current CCR, Segal-Weyl and second-quantized-spectrum proofs. H_mu separability supplies the CCR/Segal hypothesis; sigma-finiteness and finite measurable (omega,-k) supply spectrum hypotheses. Conjugate-linear annihilation after f conjugation gives complex-linear fields on invariant D_fin. Real fields have sqrt(2) Segal normalization, Weyl phase -Im<Kf,Kg> and Gaussian exp(-||Kf||^2/2). Vacuum covariance is <K conjugate(f),Kg>_2; positivity uses first test conjugate(f), not arbitrary complex diagonal. CCR commutation yields ordered Wick recursion with finite products defined on D_fin. Fixed-sector sqrt(N) bounds and continuous restriction prove all matrix coefficients tempered; restricted adjoint identities make the vacuum polynomial state positive. The injective frequency restriction for eight-variable tests preserves Schwartz decay; radial integrability establishes genuine tempered bi/relative distributions without point operators. Fock covariance follows from real affine test pullbacks and unitary lift; sector generator sums have E>=|P| including zero vacuum. AC_omega, (-+++) phase and no empirical/model-truth assertion retained. No defect found. Batch-37 suppliers are draft context, not certified by this review."
      }
