          "evidence": "Statement and the declared premises of Isotony and spacelike commutativity of scalar local Weyl algebras retain the stated choice convention. Assume Countable Choice [[def-countable-choice]]. Let $O\\subseteq\\mathbb R^4$ be open. For real $f\\in C_c^\\infty(O)$ define $$W_\\mu(f):=W_{\\rm Segal}(\\sqrt2K_\\mu f),$$ where the Segal normalization is exactly $\\Phi_{\\rm Segal}(h)=(a^\\dagger(h)+a(h))/\\sqrt2$ on the finite-particle domain, as in [[lem-qft-segal-weyl-domain]]. This scale makes the generator of $t\\mapsto W_\\mu(tf)$ equal to the real scalar field $\\Phi_\\mu(f)=a(K_\\mu f)+a^\\dagger(K_\\mu f)$ of [[lem-qft-smeared-free-scalar]]. Define the unital norm-closed operator algebra $$\\mathfrak A_\\mu(O)= \\overline{\\operatorname{alg}}^{\\|\\cdot\\|} \\{I,W_\\mu(f),W_\\mu(f)^*:f\\in C_c^\\infty(O;\\mathbb R)\\}.$$ Then $O_1\\subseteq O_2$ implies $\\mathfrak A_\\mu(O_1)\\subse This record concerns that existing premise and the fixed supplier data; it asserts no stronger choice principle or unstated family selection."
