      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-38",
        "notes": "Checked both proof paragraphs, all six direct suppliers and Fewster-Rejzner section 4.2 kernel/Weyl/local-net clauses. The Weyl generator is the closed Segal field Phi_Segal(sqrt(2)K_mu f), not the operator restricted to D_fin: even f=0 gives a zero generator on all Fock space whereas the displayed field has domain D_fin. Amended Statement to identify the self-adjoint closure and its finite-particle restriction; step 1.1 now explicitly applies the exact Segal generator supplier (new F4). Isotony follows from compact-test inclusion and norm closure. Pairwise spacelike hypotheses, CCR and causal support give Im<Kf,Kg>=0; Weyl relations then give commuting bounded generators. Inverses/adjoints, finite products and norm limits preserve cross-commutation. Empty regions generate C I and zero tests give I, so boundaries remain valid. AC_omega, sqrt(2) normalization and mathematical-only scope retained. Direct item/reference consumers: the owned correlation example uses only bounded Weyl commutation; outside pthm-qft-scalar-free-properties F9/step 1.4 and pthm-qft-free-observable-domain-limits F8/step 1.3 use only unchanged isotony/locality. Outside consumers already distinguish closures and finite-particle fields where needed; no consumer repair required and propagation stops. Reflow unchanged; precheck, rendercheck and scoped strict proof-contract passed."
