          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "Example of Positive vacuum correlation for spacelike-separated massless tests: Assume Countable Choice. In the massless model $\\mu=0$, there are nonnegative real test functions $f,g\\in C_c^\\infty(\\mathbb R^4)$ with spacelike-separated supports for which $$\\langle\\Omega,\\Phi_0(f)\\Omega\\rangle_2 =\\langle\\Omega,\\Phi_0(g)\\Omega\\rangle_2=0,\\qquad \\langle\\Omega,\\Phi_0(f)\\Phi_0(g)\\Omega\\rangle_2>0.$$ The corresponding local Weyl operators commute by [[lem-qft-scalar-local-weyl-algebra]]. The nonzero correlation is a mathematical vacuum expectation in the specified representation; it is not a measurement or a signaling effect. The specified witness, fixed coordinate space or supplied Hilbert/test objects are the inputs of this assertion; it does not assert a separate existence result after replacing them by an empty underlying set."
