        "notes": "Checked all three verification paragraphs and nine direct supplier statements. Bumps are nonnegative and nonzero with support product uniformly spacelike (D-r1-r2>2delta); positive integrals follow from continuity and nonzero values. Angular integration of e^(-epsilon|k|) d^3k/((2pi)^3 2|k|) gives 1/(4pi^2(r^2+(epsilon+i tau)^2)), with the displayed factors correct. Uniform separation bounds the denominator away from zero for epsilon down to zero. Regulated spacetime/shell exchange is absolutely integrable by compact-test L1 norms and the damped shell measure; unregulated smeared covariance converges by Hilbert Cauchy-Schwarz and dominated convergence. The limiting positive kernel has the explicit positive lower bound (integral f)(integral g)/(4pi^2(D+r1+r2)^2). Zero one-point values and bounded Weyl commutation use the exact field/locality suppliers; the amended generator domain is unused. Tong 2.165 gives two-point shell integral; Srednicki 3.15-3.19 gives normalization, not the old chapter-4 two-point locator. The massless positivity computation is local mathematics with no observation, signaling or measurement inference. Accept source-locator and proof-layout edits; no mathematical defect confirmed."
